.TH OROC-UPDATE-EXTRACT 1 "" "Oro Runtime 0.1.4" "Oro Runtime Manual"
.SH NAME
oroc\-update\-extract \- Extract a tar archive produced by update\-bundle into a destination directory.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
oroc update extract \-\-bundle=<bundle.tar> \-\-dest=<dir> [options]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Extract a tar archive produced by update\-bundle into a destination directory.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bundle=<bundle.tar>\fR
path to the tar archive to extract
.TP
\fB\-\-dest=<dir>\fR
destination directory to extract files into (created if missing)
.TP
\fB\-\-log\-file=<path>\fR
mirror logs to a JSON file
.SH NOTES
.PP
The extractor rejects absolute paths and any paths containing ".." or ':' to avoid directory traversal. Special tar entries (symlinks, devices, etc.) are ignored; regular files and directories are restored.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBoroc update extract \-\-bundle app\-1.0.0.tar \-\-dest ./update\-staging\fR
extract the contents of app\-1.0.0.tar into ./update\-staging
.SH SEE ALSO
oroc(1), oroc\-update(1)
